ptions of the event by the women competitors, in later years, state that this did not actually occur. However, eventually the officials decided that women should not run such long distances, and no women’s event longer than 200 metres would be contested in an Olympics again until " [:a {:href "/results/59982"} "1960"] ". Hitomi would return to the FSFI Women’s World Games in 1930 and win four gold medals, but she died in 1931 from tuberculosis."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "762"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69945"} "Lina Radke-Batschauer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "2:26.0 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:16.8 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "265"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/72364"} "Kinue Hitomi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "2:26.4 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "2:17.6 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "870"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75989"} "Inga Gentzel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "– (2 h1)"] [:td {} "2:17.8 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"